:5}},\"id\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm\",\"isAdvisoryBlocked\":false,\"isBlocked\":false,\"name\":\"protocol-v6-core-security-contract\",\"notes\":\"spawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-bc3052, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-bc3052)\\nImplemented the accepted schema-6 core/security contract from the verified 6308d99d... input on a clean branch rooted at required origin/main 57c1f568.... Decision and threat-boundary findings are recorded in decisions/0004 and TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md. This is a documentation-only owned scope: schemas/vectors/tests are downstream-owned and were not edited; existing validation passed. The host Python initially lacked jsonschema, so validation used a task-local venv populated from pinned requirements-dev.txt.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-bc3052, pid=1744, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-9fca47, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-9fca47)\\nReview verdict: changes requested. protocol/core.md weakens two accepted MUST-level details: bootstrap probes do not explicitly use a manager-owned empty CWD with GOENV=off and GOTOOLCHAIN=local in the bootstrap environment, and go-list trust does not require the accepted Standard \\u0026\\u0026 Goroot conjunction. Full evidence and green validation results are in TASK-260720-1nvomm_review-verdict.md. Route to documentation rework, then a new reviewer cycle.\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-9fca47, pid=16192, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-d7e0fe, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-d7e0fe)\\nReviewer rework applied in protocol/core.md: bootstrap probes now use a manager-owned empty CWD with private roots, GOENV=off, GOTOOLCHAIN=local, normalized locale, and no inherited GOROOT/target; go-list toolchain trust now requires Standard == true and Goroot == true. Scoped validator and full make validate pass in the pinned task-local venv; git diff --check passes. Updated TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md and TASK-260720-1nvomm_validation.log with exact evidence.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn completion blocked: no new task-scoped outcome artifact was attached. Add an outcome resource named like TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md and then set status back to to-review.\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-d7e0fe, pid=24410, exit=0)\\nOrchestrator recovery: content rework is complete and validated, but RUN-260720-d7e0fe could not hand off because it updated existing outcome resources instead of attaching a distinct new task-scoped rework outcome. Add a new TASK-260720-1nvomm_rework-1.md outcome resource containing the two corrections and exact validation evidence; do not change project files unless evidence is inaccurate; then route to to-review.\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-b95c7d, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-b95c7d)\\nRecovery audit confirmed both reviewer-requested MUST-level corrections and found one additional accepted-contract gap: dependency command narrowing still said script-only. protocol/core.md now permits schema-6 build commands while explicitly retaining script-only behavior for schemas 1 through 5. Evidence is attached as TASK-260720-1nvomm_rework-1.md; scoped and combined validation gates pass.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-b95c7d, pid=37242, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-e7562d, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-e7562d)\\nFinal review verdict: accepted. All acceptance criteria and