xecutable names and output selection. Prefer logical target IDs plus manager-derived command name and private staging path unless evidence supports another closed design. Audit must happen before any compiler execution. Repository access failure must warn during offline/static check when verification cannot be attempted and must fail install before mutation when source cannot be resolved. Credentials and signing identities must never come from the package descriptor. Research authoritative Git, Go build, platform signing/notarization and sandbox constraints as needed. Persist the decision and threat model as a new task-scoped outcome resource, include concrete JSON examples and normative MUST/MUST NOT recommendations, record source links, then route to to-review for an independent architecture review.\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-482663, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-482663)\\nArchitecture logbook 2026-07-27 — resolved the external build-repository scope delta without editing project/spec files. Recommendation: freeze schema 6/go-v1; add schema 7, strict build_repositories, locked Git commit with optional tag assertion, curator-build.json schema 1 logical targets, new closed go-repository-v1, receipt v2, marker v3, and claim v3/rc.5. Repository targets cannot select executable names, output paths, argv, environment, credentials, signing, hooks, or plugins; manifest command keys and manager-private staging remain authoritative. Exact external snapshots must be raw-tree validated and independently audited before cache lookup/compiler on real, cache-hit, dry-run, install/repair/audit paths; syntax-o